{"hash":"37251f3a9131d9d4","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":77.921,"said":"Walk slowly here, where the line moves towards the temple, and let me tell you of Veer Hamirji Gohil. He was a young prince of Lathi in Saurashtra, remembered for riding out to defend Somnath when an army of the Delhi Sultanate came to this shore. Accounts differ on which raid it was: some say Alauddin Khalji’s, in 1299; others, the governor Zafar Khan’s, about a century later. On one thing they all agree: he did not come back. Beside him fought Vegadaji Bhil, a chieftain of the forests, and their friendship is still honoured here, the hills and the court standing together. The old songs of Saurashtra add more. They say Hamirji married Vegadaji’s daughter just before the battle, and that even after his head fell, he fought on before the temple. Hold those as the songs hold them: as devotion, more than record. His memorial stands at the temple’s entrance, and pilgrims bow to it on their way in. Every step of this walk passes through a gateway that someone once gave everything to keep open.\n\nDid you know? In January 2026 the Shaurya Yatra of the Somnath Swabhiman Parv set out from Veer Hamirji Gohil’s statue.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1003},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1019,"end":1124}],"words":[[0.098,0.264,0,4],[0.374,0.505,5,11],[0.891,0.337,12,16],[1.504,0.168,18,23],[1.685,0.084,24,27],[1.781,0.3,28,32],[2.093,0.361,33,38],[2.466,0.397,39,46],[2.874,0.108,47,50],[2.995,0.505,51,57],[3.776,0.18,59,62],[3.968,0.24,63,66],[4.221,0.12,67,69],[4.353,0.276,70,74],[4.641,0.18,75,78],[4.834,0.216,79,81],[5.062,0.252,82,86],[5.326,0.529,87,94],[5.867,0.505,95,100],[7.272,0.108,102,104],[7.392,0.18,105,108],[7.584,0.084,109,110],[7.68,0.325,111,116],[8.017,0.288,117,123],[8.317,0.144,124,126],[8.474,0.385,127,132],[8.87,0.168,133,135],[9.05,0.721,136,146],[9.964,0.553,148,158],[10.529,0.18,159,162],[10.721,0.325,163,169],[11.058,0.204,170,173],[11.274,0.072